.TH "SPGEN-SCHEMA" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-schema \- Generates OpenAPI schemas documenting an endpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.schema [options] <READ\-MODEL|COMMAND|QUERY>
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenAPI documents for the endpoint: the request body, the response envelope, the query parameters. OpenApiSpex modules, referenced from the controller's operation; there is nothing to register in the API spec — using them is the registration.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the command, query or read model.
.IP \[bu] 2
The public API (../domain/public\-api.md) function exists — its @spec is the shape a response schema is derived from.
.SH "What the generator does"
By element kind (the \-\-template is derived, as everywhere):
.PP
\fIElement, Schema files\fR
.TP
\fBread model\fR
.br
<DomainObject>Response and <DomainObject>CollectionResponse, both built from the JSON:API view (Sportipedia.Support.JSONAPI.OpenApiSchema)
.TP
\fBcommand (create, update)\fR
.br
<Command>Request from the command's data fields
.TP
\fBcommand (delete)\fR
.br
none — the id rides in the body as data.id
.TP
\fBquery (collection, with parameters)\fR
.br
<Operation>QueryParams, built from the view and the query's declared filterable/sortable names (OpenApiSchema.query_params/2)
.PP
Both JSON:API halves are derived, not transcribed: from_view/2 for the response document, query_params/2 for the request parameters. The same names also gate the request — the controller's JSONAPI.QueryParser options come from the same two model lists — so a filterable or sortable field is stated once in the model and appears twice, as a validation and as a contract. A body that spells its members out by hand is reported Outdated: the merge never rewrites it, and the model is where the fix belongs.
.PP
What the query's parameters must state:
.PP
\fIMember, From\fR
.TP
\fBfilter\fR
.br
parameters.properties.filter.properties — each field's description is the documented one
.TP
\fBsort\fR
.br
parameters.properties.sort.sortableFields, in the order the model lists them; falling back to the filterable fields when the model names none
.TP
\fBpage\fR
.br
parameters.properties.page.properties: number/size → :numbered, limit/offset → :offset, no page → the member is not documented
.TP
\fBfields\fR
.br
the view's fields/0, keyed by its type/0 — nothing to state
.PP
Two rules worth knowing because they are easy to get wrong by hand:
.IP \[bu] 2
A create request never carries id: the public API generates it.
.IP \[bu] 2
Types follow the model, not the Elixir struct: string/uuid → :string with the format, integer → :integer, nullable when the field is optional.
.SH Tests
Each schema module gets its own ExUnit test file (use ExUnit.Case, no DB, no sandbox) asserting the structure of schema/0: its title (<composite>.<SchemaName>) and that it is an object. Behaviour is asserted at the endpoint (./endpoint\-test.md), not in the schema.
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia_web/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/schemas/<schema>.ex (OpenAPI schema per shape)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia_web/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/schemas/<schema>_test.exs (field coverage per schema)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
what the operation does: create|update|delete|none|read|collection (optional: the model declares the operation for this element)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
create
.IP \(bu 2
update
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.IP \(bu 2
none
.IP \(bu 2
read
.IP \(bu 2
collection
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREAD\-MODEL|COMMAND|QUERY\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: endpoint, feature
